<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ernest, Duke of Saxe-Hildburghausen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1655">1655</a>–<a href="/years/1715">1715</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ernest, Duke of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hildburghausen">Hildburghausen</a>, was the sixth son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-i-duke-of-saxe-gotha">Ernest the Pious</a> of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a>. In the partition of his father's inheritance in 1680 he received Hildburghausen in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, made the small town his residence and founded the line of Saxe-Hildburghausen. He built a palace and welcomed Huguenot refugees to the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ernest-duke-of-saxe-hildburghausen.jpg" alt="Ernest, Duke of Saxe-Hildburghausen" width="320" height="494" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wolfgang Philipp Kilian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arolsen_Klebeband_01_175_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
